Z||000004||frontal lobe||12-19-2001||12:15 PM||||Yea, I'm with ray b on this one.  To me, driving through Atlanta is like NASCAR.  Bumper to bumper, swapping paint, drafting, bold moves, runnin' 3-wide (on 2 lanes).<P>But maybe, like nascar, their fatalities are not high when they crash.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||12-19-2001||12:29 PM||||I *ahem* drive in Atlanta every day. <BR>I am also amazed that we are not on the list.<P>Perhaps it's because most everybody here drives SUVs. When they hit something, they just tear whatever they hit to pieces, but don't die. <P>I don't think BMW's or Benz's sold in Atlanta have turn signals. I've never seen any evidence of it, anyway. Azzholes. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Blacktree||12-19-2001||01:50 PM||||Wow, 5 of the 10 worst cities are in Florida. Although, having witnessed the traffic in Florida first-hand for about 15 years, I can agree with those figures.<P>I live fairly close to the tourism district (about 10 miles E of Disney). Every day on my drive to and from work (no I don't work for Disney), I see at least one auto accident. About once a week, one of the accidents will be bad enough for 911 to be called. With this many auto accidents, it's no surprise that more people are getting killed on our roads down here.<P>I can attribute a large number of the auto accidents to 2 things :<P>1) Tourist from another country who has no freaking idea how to drive on the right side of the road, much less the other traffic laws. We Americans have to pass a driving test to get a license, but the foreigners just plop down some money for a rental car and have at it.<P>2) A local driving like Mario Andretti in order to get to work on time. For some reason, the locals have the "speed racer syndrome". They think they're doing something wrong if they go less than 15MPH over the speed limit. They also make a point of doing everything exactly the opposite of what is written in the Florida Driver's Handbook.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.tweaktech.com" TARGET=_blank>Tweaktech</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||OcalaFiero||12-19-2001||03:29 PM||||It's the tourists and the Snow-Birds (Old people wintering down here) killing themselves off in traffic accidents down here. But hey, it's just another case of natural selection.<P>Mike<BR>Ocala, Florida<BR><p>[This message has been edited by OcalaFiero (edited 12-19-2001).]||||reg||1
